@crew marrow
// SW5, the endgame pool (plans/ending-spec.html section 9): said only after you choose to stay. Every line is
// gated by the bare condition "endgame" (EN2 adds it to the line filter, section 22); "endgame:early" marks the
// lines that only make sense in the first two weeks after you stay (RV21).

== greet
? endgame:early
- {hi}. I half expected an empty chair at breakfast. Then there you were.   #warm
? endgame weekday:thu time:evening
- Thursday. The piano. Sit at the back if you like. Everyone does, very quietly.

== chat
? endgame:early
- Headquarters wrote again. A very polite letter. I wrote back a politer one.   #funny
? endgame:early
- The Admiral took your news calmly. He takes everything calmly. It's his great gift.   #funny
? endgame
- No more ladders to climb. So tell me. What does a Tuesday look like, now?
- I asked you one question in your first week. Here's another. What does the ship need next?
? endgame tier>=friend
- Your page in my little book ran over. I've started you on page forty-one.   #warm

== life
? endgame tier>=friend
- My daughter asked who the cadet was who stayed. I said: one of ours. She understood.   #warm
? endgame beat:marrow.5
- We've both turned down a post now, you and I. That makes a club. A small one, with a step.   #funny

== bye
? endgame
- Go on, then. The ship isn't going anywhere. Neither are you, I'm told.   #funny
